# Copy this file to `.env` locally, or set these as environment variables
# in your hosting provider (Netlify, etc), to activate the contact form's
# email delivery (src/lib/mailer.ts). Never commit a real `.env` file —
# it's already covered by .gitignore.
#
# Without these set, the form still works end-to-end: it validates input
# and submits, but tells the visitor that automatic sending isn't
# configured yet and points them to CONTACT_TO / SITE.email directly,
# instead of silently pretending the message was sent.
#
# Works with any SMTP mailbox — nothing here is provider-specific. For
# Studio VM's OVH mailbox (Zimbra), the typical settings are:
#   SMTP_HOST=ssl0.ovh.net
#   SMTP_PORT=465
# Confirm the exact hostname/port for your mailbox in the OVH manager
# (Web Cloud > Emails > your domain > Configuration du logiciel de
# messagerie) before relying on the values above.

SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=

# Where contact-form submissions are delivered. Falls back to SITE.email
# in src/lib/constants.ts if unset.
CONTACT_TO=contact@studiovm-design.fr
